{
  "id": "calc1.derivatives.tangent-cubic",
  "course": "calc1",
  "topic": "derivatives",
  "kind": "tangent_line",
  "title": "Tangent line to a cubic",
  "prompt": "Find the equation of the tangent line to $f(x) = x^3 - 2x$ at $x = 1$.",
  "answer_format": "An equation like y = mx + b.",
  "difficulty": 1,
  "tags": [
    "tangent line"
  ],
  "data": {
    "function": "x^3 - 2x",
    "var": "x",
    "at": "1"
  },
  "answer": "y = x - 2",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "You need a point (1, f(1)) and a slope f′(1).",
    "Point-slope form: y − f(a) = f′(a)(x − a)."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "$f(1) = 1 - 2 = -1$, so the point is $(1, -1)$.",
    "$f'(x) = 3x^2 - 2$, so the slope is $f'(1) = 1$.",
    "$y - (-1) = 1(x - 1)$, i.e. $y = x - 2$."
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "openstax-calc1",
    "section": "3.1 Defining the Derivative",
    "note": "Original problem; see tangent lines."
  },
  "review": {
    "status": "draft"
  },
